ecision record for issue #5852 (from parent issue #5679): `doc/2026-11-08_decision_id5852_native_rendering_os_standard_controls.md`.\n\n- **Control selection (§2):** every semantic element kind maps to the OS-standard control for Mac (AppKit/SwiftUI), Windows (WinUI), and GNOME (GTK 4 / libadwaita); the renderer configures standard controls, never re-implements or redraws them.\n- **Assertion mapping (§3):** every style-assertion dimension in the settled issue #5850 vocabulary (tone/colour roles, text/typography roles, emphasis, density, gap/pad spacing, corner, elevation, states) maps per platform, or is marked an explicit **platform-default** with the coverage-tooling warning — no silent drops.\n- **Platform-conflict rule (§4), stated as a decision:** platform wins for behaviour and accessibility; the assertion wins for identity, subject to platform clamps — and every clamp/substitution is reported by tooling.\n- **Assumptions (§1):** parent issue #5679 and markup-vocabulary issue #5849 are not settled yet; the record states its assumptions against both explicitly (following the issue #5850 and issue #5853 record precedents) and changes no parent decision. Invariants (§5) are the conformance oracle; alternatives (§6) and follow-ons (§8) are recorded.\n\nDesign-only change; no code or tests are affected. Verification is the record's coverage: every #5850 dimension and every platform named in issue #5852 is mapped or explicitly platform-defaulted, and no parent decision is silently changed.\n\nCloses #5852\n\nQueue: task 13953 (repo-health-code-pilot), lane code-j.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796782062&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7912&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7912&signature=61a382ccd32de3b2127365465fc2514f45e4351060519267cb3d7e9dba4160f4\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-colo